  "articleBody": "Remodel framing can be an exciting part of transforming your space, but sometimes you hit a snag that makes you wonder if you're on the right track. One common issue is starting demolition only to find electrical or plumbing lines exactly where you planned your new opening. This is a clear sign that you might need professional help to safely reroute utilities without causing damage. Another big problem arises when you’re dealing with what you suspect might be a load-bearing wall. If you cut into it and realize it's supporting a significant part of your home, that's a major red flag that you need an expert to assess the situation and ensure structural integrity. Also, if you've tried to frame an opening and it just doesn’t seem square, plumb, or level, or if your measurements aren’t matching up with the new window or door, it's time to pause. An improperly framed opening can lead to installation issues, drafts, and even problems with the window or door operating correctly. If you're seeing unexpected damage to nearby framing or finishes as you work, or if you're just unsure about how to properly size a new opening without compromising the existing structure, those are all signals. When your remodel involves structural changes, concealed utilities, or corrections to an opening that's already out of spec, a qualified professional from HH Remodeling LLC can step in, diagnose the problem, and get your project back on track. Don't let a snag turn into a full-blown disaster; call us at 303-505-0866 for expert assistance.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}